From 8f87d4a76e7a95c133a40666bc38a727246b0d68 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Opus 5.5" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 03:35:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] x11: list RandR 1.5 monitors, not CRTCs

available_monitors listed one monitor per active CRTC. Since RandR
1.5 the server has monitors of its own, which are what `xrandr
--listmonitors` shows and what Xinerama, and so the window manager,
goes by: usually one per CRTC, but a screen split with `xrandr
--setmonitor` (an ultrawide used as two, a single framebuffer under
Xvfb or a virtual X server) is several monitors on one CRTC, or on
none. winit saw only the CRTC, so such a monitor could not be named,
and Fullscreen::Borderless, which moves the window to the monitor's
origin before asking the window manager for fullscreen, always sent
the window to the CRTC's origin: a window fullscreened from the right
half of a split screen went fullscreen on the left half.

Where the server has RandR 1.5 (winit now asks for that version
rather than 1.3), the list is RRGetMonitors' active monitors, in the
server's order, each with its own name, position, size, physical size
(for the scale factor) and primary flag, and the CRTC that shows its
first output for the refresh rate and video modes. A monitor that is
only part of its CRTC offers no video modes, since setting one would
change every monitor on the CRTC, and a monitor no CRTC shows has
CRTC 0 and none either. MonitorHandle's identity is the CRTC and the
monitor's name atom together, so the monitors of one CRTC are told
apart and a monitor with no CRTC is not taken for the dummy. Where
the server is older, or lists no monitor, the CRTC list is as before.

get_output_info is split into the output's modes and the scale factor
of a size, so that a monitor's own size gives its scale factor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/changelog/unreleased.md b/src/changelog/unreleased.md
index 9b1f363..f5e747b 100644
--- a/src/changelog/unreleased.md
+++ b/src/changelog/unreleased.md
@@ -50,3 +50,4 @@ changelog entry.
 - On X11, fix a panic in `Window::inner_size` and other getters when another client destroyed the window.
 - On Wayland, fix `Window::set_cursor` copying a custom cursor into a new buffer when it is already the window's cursor, and panicking when the buffer could not be allocated.
 - On X11, `Window::is_minimized` and `Window::is_maximized` no longer make a round trip to the X server on every call; `_NET_WM_STATE` is kept until a `PropertyNotify` says it changed.
+- On X11, list the RandR 1.5 monitors (those of `xrandr --listmonitors`, which the window manager goes by) where the server has them, rather than one per CRTC, so that `Fullscreen::Borderless` reaches each monitor of a screen split with `xrandr --setmonitor`.
